# Line endings are not cosmetic for files a Linux shell executes.
#
# With `core.autocrlf=true` -- the Git for Windows default -- a Windows
# checkout rewrote `oms/entrypoint.sh` with CRLF. The image still built; the
# container then died immediately with
#
#     exec /app/entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory
#
# because the kernel reads the shebang literally and looks for an interpreter
# named "/bin/sh\r". The error names the script, not the line ending, which is
# why this is worth pinning rather than remembering. Anyone cloning on Windows
# hits it, and until this file existed the answer was that the container simply
# could not be built here.
*.sh text eol=lf
scripts/hooks/* text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf
entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
